schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Bitcoin's genesis block embeds a Times of London bailout headline"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Satoshi Nakamoto mined Bitcoin's genesis block on January 3, 2009,
    creating 50 BTC, and embedded within it a headline from The Times of
    London: "Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks."
  evidence: >-
    Stated as historical fact in the article's "January 2009: The Launch"
    section; this specific fact is extremely widely documented in Bitcoin
    historiography (the headline is visible in the actual genesis block's
    coinbase transaction on-chain), though the article itself lists no
    dedicated source or reference for it.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/bitcoin-history.md
  interpretation: >-
    The article reads the embedded headline as "a timestamp and a quiet
    statement about why Bitcoin mattered" — framing Bitcoin's origin as a
    direct response to the 2008 financial-crisis bank bailouts.
  uncertainty: >-
    The underlying fact (headline text and date) is independently verifiable
    on the Bitcoin blockchain itself and is not contested in the broader
    literature; however this article carries no citation for it, and its own
    frontmatter lists placeholder/garbage source values (see companion
    signal object on this work order).
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/bitcoin-history.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-648651c05dac
